 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Procurement Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is procurement automation?\", \"a\": \"Procurement automation is software that runs a company's buying steps by its written policy instead of by email. Requests reach the right approvers, quotes are collected, orders go to suppliers, and spend is checked against contracts, with every decision on record.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you build procure to pay automation?\", \"a\": \"Write down your thresholds, approvers, and contracted suppliers, then describe them to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a>. It builds the request form and the routing behind it, issues each purchase order, and connects to your ledger. Run a month of past requests through it before your team relies on it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the role of AI in procurement automation?\", \"a\": \"AI handles the parts of buying that arrive as loose text. A request typed as one sentence or a quote sent as an attachment becomes structured fields a rule can act on, like category and amount. The approval rules themselves stay as fixed numbers your team sets, such as finance sign-off above $25,000.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is digital procurement the same as procurement automation?\", \"a\": \"No. Digital procurement is the wider shift of sourcing, purchasing, contracts, and invoice handling onto software and shared data. Procurement automation is one part of it: steps that run with no one pushing them, like routing a request or chasing a slow approver. Turning an approved request into a supplier order is the job of purchase order automation.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a procurement system and procurement automation?\", \"a\": \"A procurement system is where buying records live: suppliers, requisitions, purchase orders, and contract terms. Procurement automation is the behavior on top of those records. Each request moves through its approval workflow without anyone forwarding it, and an order placed off contract is flagged the week it happens.\"}, {\"q\": \"What types of technology are used in procurement automation?\", \"a\": \"Most setups pair a workflow engine that routes approvals with a catalog of contracted items for ordering. Document reading pulls fields out of quotes and invoices. A connection to the accounting system keeps vendor records and cost centers matched. Emergent writes all of it as one app, and paid plans let you export the code to GitHub.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the best procurement automation software?\", \"a\": \"Choose by where your buying stalls. A team running formal sourcing events across hundreds of suppliers needs a full procurement suite. A team whose requests sit in inboxes needs intake, approval routing, and a weekly spend check set to its own thresholds. Emergent builds that smaller set from a description of your policy, and approvers are never billed as seats.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the stages of procure to pay automation?\", \"a\": \"Procure to pay runs through requisition, approval, purchase order, goods receipt, invoice, and payment. Start automating at the front, where requests wait on approvers. Later, add three-way matching: before payment, each invoice is checked against its PO, then against the receiving record. That end of the cycle is accounts payable automation.\"}, {\"q\": \"What types of procurement work best with procurement automation?\", \"a\": \"Start with indirect procurement, such as software and office supplies. These are many small purchases that follow a few rules. Direct procurement buys the materials that go into what you sell, and it runs on production forecasts. Bring it in once the rules for indirect buying hold up for a quarter.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is left for buyers after procurement automation?\", \"a\": \"Buyers keep the work that needs judgment: negotiating with suppliers, planning each category, and settling cases a rule cannot. A sole-source request or a supplier that missed two delivery dates still needs a person. Routing and reminders move to the app, and every exception reaches its owner with the request history attached.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
